// A tuplet in the LOWER voice: its "3" bracket must sit BELOW the triplet (the
// voice's stem side, voice 2 = stems down), anchored to voice 2's own notes —
// not above by the staff-wide "multi-voice => bracket up" rule, and not on the
// primary voice's noteheads. Also guards that voice 2's triplet still beams
// separately from the eighths after it — ⚠️ not because a tuplet's edge cuts a
// beam (that rule was an invention and is gone), but because the exception LOOKUP
// changes with the run's shortest duration: the triplet's twelfths take 4/4's 1/12
// entry and end at the quarter, the plain eighths take the 1/8 entry and run to the
// half measure. Three beams: 3, then 2, then 4.
// LILYPOND-REF: lily/tuplet-bracket.cc get_default_dir — bracket on the stem side.
octave absolute
title "Lower-voice tuplet"
part mel { clef treble }
section S {
  mel {
    voice { c''4 c'' c'' c'' | }
    { tuplet 3/2 { e'8 f' g' } a' b' c'' b' a' g' | }
  }
}
form main { S }
score main "multivoice-voice2-tuplet" { staff mel }

